# About the developer

- **Experience:** Beginner — no prior coding background. Explain changes in plain language; avoid jargon or define it briefly.
- **Workflow:** Edits happen in this folder (`jbe` / `japan-evangelistic-band` on GitHub). Push to GitHub only when explicitly asked (e.g. "push", "save to GitHub", "publish").
- **Hosting & testing:** Game is hosted on **GitHub Pages**; primary testing is on **iPhone** (Add to Home Screen PWA). **Live URL:** https://spellmynameright.github.io/japan-evangelistic-band/ (not `claude-mobile`). Edits need **push** then refresh. If the phone shows an old build, use Settings → **Load latest update** (Build number in settings) or delete the Home Screen app and re-add from the correct URL.
- **AI tools:** Uses **Cursor** (implementation, git) and **Claude** (planning, design). Both should read `CLAUDE.md`; Cursor also loads `.cursor/rules/`.
- **GitHub:** Account `spellmynameright`, repo `japan-evangelistic-band`. GitHub CLI is authenticated on this machine.
- **Domain knowledge:** Real missionary experience in Japan — authenticity in tone, mechanics, and cultural details matters.

When teaching or proposing changes: small steps, say what file you touched and why. After JSON/balance edits, offer to push so they can test on the phone — that is their usual workflow.
